[; cx-stdlib/supervise — restart policies over monitored workers
   (spec/03-approved/std-lib/supervise.md, band CXER5090-5109;
   issue #765, RULED: SUP-1). PURE CX over shipped primitives:
   [?worker]/[?monitor] (code.md §10.4.6/.6a — terminal events delivered
   even post-mortem), fan-out channels (U1.11a), and cx-stdlib/sched
   timers (backoff/window/attempt-reset ride the mock clock, so restart
   fixtures are deterministic). It adds NO new concurrency primitive and
   NO capability (§5) — the module is the restart LOOP written once,
   with policies as data.

   SHAPE. One supervision loop per supervisor, running in an ordinary
   [?worker]. The loop parks on ONE subscription to its own fan-out
   inbox; everything that needs its attention arrives as an inbox
   message: control ops from the public verbs ([sup-op ...] with an
   embedded reply channel), terminal notes from the child-body wrapper
   ([sup-note ...] — the wrapper catches the child fn's fault, posts the
   note, then re-raises so the worker terminal stays honest), and sched
   [tick ...] posts for backoff delays, intensity-window expiry, and
   per-child attempt-reset. Closing the handle ([?with-open]) closes
   that inbox subscription — the parked loop wakes closed-and-drained
   and runs the same graceful stop as supervise/stop.

   CHILD SPECS carry the body as a child element (attrs are scalar-only,
   code.md §6.4.1 — RULED: SUP-1 rider SUP-1c):
     [child name="ing" restart=:permanent shutdown=5s [fn $callable]]
   restart ∈ :permanent (any exit) | :transient (panic only) |
   :temporary (never). POLICY is data:
     [policy strategy=:one-for-one max-restarts=5 window=1m
       backoff=:exp base=100ms cap=10s]
   strategy ∈ :one-for-one | :one-for-all | :rest-for-one. Defaults
   (SUP-1h): :one-for-one, max-restarts=3, window=5s, backoff=:none,
   base=100ms, cap=10s, shutdown=5s. Intensity counts POLICY DECISIONS
   (a one-for-all flap of N children = 1), never respawns; only
   policy-initiated restarts count — a supervisor-initiated cancel is
   never a countable exit and never restarts :transient children.

   GIVE-UP (§4.3): past max-restarts within window the loop cancels all
   children (reverse start order, bounded), emits [gave-up ...] as the
   final event, and terminates with cx-err:CXER5094 — a parent
   supervisor monitoring this one sees [panicked ... [err CXER0220
   [cause [err CXER5094]]]] and applies ITS policy (SUP-1g). Escalation
   is composition, not a feature.

   EVENTS are a standard keep=256 fan-out subscription of the
   supervisor's own acts, replayed from the retained floor:
     [child-started name= attempt=] [child-exited name= reason=(:done|
     :panicked|:cancelled) err-code=?] [child-restarted name= attempt=
     delay-ms=] [child-abandoned name=] [gave-up restarts= window-ms=]
   A laggard observer hits the channel contract's CXER0218 STREAM_GAP
   and re-subscribes (SUP-1b). STATUS answers through the control
   round-trip while running and stays readable after stop through the
   keep=1 status cell (SUP-1a — status is impure; purity is enforced,
   CXER0233, and reading live state is channel I/O by construction).

   FOUR-CHANNEL MODEL (code.md §9.1.2): the running supervisor and its
   status snapshot are present VALUES; a malformed policy/spec is
   CXER5090 and a duplicate child CXER5091 (faults); stop of an
   already-stopped supervisor is a VALUE (null; idempotent) and
   stop-child of an unknown name is the VALUE false — but
   start-child/stop-child/events on a STOPPED supervisor are the fault
   CXER5093 (status stays readable). CXER5092 is reserved. The give-up
   terminal is CXER5094 on the loop worker.

   The abandon rule (§4.4): stopping a child is [?cancel] + a wait
   bounded by its shutdown; a child that outlives the bound is ABANDONED
   ([child-abandoned], state abandoned), never force-killed (force-kill
   does not exist; cancellation is cooperative, §10.5.4). On the
   reference substrate the cancel terminal is stamped at request
   (SUP-1f), so the bound resolves immediately and abandon is reserved
   surface; the no-hang guarantee holds either way.

   NOTE: this const is the loader source of truth for cx-stdlib/supervise. ]

[?lib 'cx-stdlib/sched']
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/time']
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/fp']

# ── utilities ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# sup--alloc mints a process-unique id, used to name this supervisor's four
# channels and its loop worker (RULED: SPF-1, issue #895). The source is the
# EVALUATOR's own handle counter: [?subscribe] stamps every subscription with
# a `__cx_close_id__` drawn from the monotonic per-evaluator allocator the
# engine keeps precisely to tell handles apart. [?channel]/[?subscribe]/
# [?close] are CORE directives (code.md §10.4) — present in every §4 profile
# and carrying NO capability, which is what the module's §5 no-capability
# contract requires. The generator channel is one fixed-name, never-read
# rendezvous shared by every call; the subscription is closed at once, so
# nothing accumulates.
#
# It used to arm a 240-hour [$sched:after] against a devnull channel, cancel
# it, and keep the TIMER'S synthesized name — i.e. it borrowed the scheduler
# registry's private counter, from an OPTIONAL local-effect pack, for a need
# that has nothing to do with scheduling. In a `-d cx_no_pack_sched` build
# that name came back empty and the failure surfaced 25 fixtures deep as
# `[?channel] requires :name`. cx-stdlib/uuid is NOT the replacement: its
# v4/v7 generators are capability-gated on `random`, and supervise grants no
# capability.
[?def sup--alloc scope=private impure [returns string] ()
  [?let [= $gen [?channel name="cxsup-idgen" sharing=independent retention=window keep=1]]
    [= $s [?subscribe from=$gen]]
    [= $id [$concat "" $s@__cx_close_id__]]
    [= $_ [?close $s]]
    $id]]

# sup--has-sched reports whether the `sched` local-effect pack is in THIS
# build (RULED: SPF-1(b)). [$sched:clock-mode] is the cheapest honest probe —
# pure, nullary, no timer armed, no registry touched; where the pack is
# excluded the callable is simply absent and the call refuses.
#
# The probe's RESULT is consumed on purpose. A `[?let]` binding is LAZY: an
# earlier spelling here bound [$sched:clock-mode] to an unread $_m and
# answered a constant `true`, so the call never happened and the refusal
# below was dead code in exactly the build it exists for. Comparing the
# rendered mode forces the call, which is the whole point of the probe.
[?def sup--has-sched scope=private impure [returns bool] ()
  [?fallback [not [= [$concat "" [$sched:clock-mode]] ""]]
    [recover-with false]]]

[?def sup--is-err scope=private pure [returns bool] ($v)
  [?match $v [case [err] true] [else false]]]

[?def sup--append scope=private pure [returns any] ($a $b)
  [$fp:flat-map ($a, $b) [?fn ($s) $s]]]

[?def sup--reverse scope=private pure [returns any] ($s)
  [?if [$empty $s]
    [then ()]
    [else [?let [= $t [$tail $s]]
      [= $rt [sup--reverse $t]]
      [= $h [$first $s]]
      [= $hw [$fp:pure $h]]
      [sup--append $rt $hw]]]]]

[?def sup--dur-ms scope=private impure [returns int] ($d)
  [?fallback [$time:duration-total-ms $d]
    [recover-with
      [?let [= $s [$concat "" $d]]
        [= $p [$time:parse-duration $s]]
        [$time:duration-total-ms $p]]]]]

[?def sup--pow2 scope=private pure [returns int] ($n::int)
  [?if [< $n 1] [then 1]
    [else [?if [> $n 30] [then 1073741824]
      [else [?let [= $r [sup--pow2 [- $n 1]]] [* 2 $r]]]]]]]

[?def sup--member scope=private pure [returns bool] ($names $x)
  [?let [= $hits [?for [in $n $names] [where [= $n $x]] [yield $n]]]
    [> [$count $hits] 0]]]

# rebuild one child record with a new state (everything else carried)
[?def sup--rec-with scope=private pure [returns map] ($c::map $state::string $wname::string $attempt::int $spawns::int $mon $w)
  {'name': $c/name 'fn': $c/fn 'restart': $c/restart 'shutdown-ms': $c/shutdown-ms
   'wname': $wname 'attempt': $attempt 'spawns': $spawns 'state': $state 'mon': $mon 'w': $w}]

[?def sup--rec-state scope=private pure [returns map] ($c::map $state::string)
  [sup--rec-with $c $state $c/wname $c/attempt $c/spawns $c/mon $c/w]]

[?def sup--st-set scope=private pure [returns map] ($st::map $children $pends $decisions::int $gave-up::bool)
  {'sid': $st/sid 'inbox': $st/inbox 'isub': $st/isub 'events': $st/events 'statusch': $st/statusch
   'sleepch': $st/sleepch 'strategy': $st/strategy 'max-restarts': $st/max-restarts
   'window-ms': $st/window-ms 'backoff': $st/backoff 'base-ms': $st/base-ms 'cap-ms': $st/cap-ms
   'children': $children 'pends': $pends 'decisions': $decisions 'gave-up': $gave-up}]

# ── status cell ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

[?def sup--snapshot scope=private pure [returns element] ($children $decisions::int)
  [?let [= $rows [?for [in $c $children]
      [yield [child name=$c/name state=$c/state attempts=$c/attempt]]]]
    [supervisor-status restarts-in-window=$decisions $rows]]]

[?def sup--publish scope=private impure [returns null] ($statusch $children $decisions::int)
  [?let [= $snap [sup--snapshot $children $decisions]]
    [= $_ [?send $snap to=$statusch]]
    null]]

[?def sup--read-cell scope=private impure [returns element] ($statusch)
  [?let [= $try [?subscribe from=$statusch from-pos=0]]
    [= $sub [?if [sup--is-err $try]
        [then [?subscribe from=$statusch from-pos=$try@floor]]
        [else $try]]]
    [= $batch [?receive from=$sub max=64 deadline=0]]
    [= $n [$count $batch]]
    [= $_c [?close $sub]]
    [?if [< $n 1]
      [then [err code=cx-err:CXER5090 message='E_SUP_ARG_INVALID: not a supervisor handle (no status cell)']]
      [else [$nth $batch $n]]]]]

# ── the child body wrapper ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

[?def sup--child-body scope=private impure [returns any] ($fn $name::string $wname::string $inbox)
  [?fallback
    [?let [= $r [$fn]]
      [= $bad [sup--is-err $r]]
      [; #908 — a child that RETURNS an [err] value is just as dead as one
         that raises, and its error is just as real. This arm used to
         `[skip]`, so the only terminal signal was one carrying no [err]:
         the supervisor saw outcome=:panicked with an EMPTY error filter,
         and building `err-code=` from `[$first ()]` hit the engine's
         (correct) refusal to write an attribute from the empty sequence.
         Post the same note the raise path posts, paired with the returned
         err, so both deaths carry their cause. Defaulting err-code to ""
         instead would have asserted that something panicked for no stated
         reason — the parent reading this stream for escalation must not
         confuse "no cause given" with "cause is X". ]
      [= $_n [?if $bad
        [then [?send ([sup-note name=$name wname=$wname outcome=:panicked], $r) to=$inbox]]
        [else [?send ([sup-note name=$name wname=$wname outcome=:done]) to=$inbox]]]]
      $r]
    [recover-with
      [?if [= $err@code 'cx-err:CXER0260']
        [then $err]
        [else [?let [= $_n [?send ([sup-note name=$name wname=$wname outcome=:panicked], $err) to=$inbox]]
          $err]]]]]]

# ── spawn / stop one child ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

[?def sup--spawn scope=private impure [returns map] ($sid::string $inbox $events $rec::map $attempt::int)
  [?let [= $name $rec/name]
    [= $spawns [+ $rec/spawns 1]]
    [= $wname [$concat "cxsup-" $sid "-" $name "-s" $spawns]]
    [= $fn $rec/fn]
    [= $w [?worker name=$wname [sup--child-body $fn $name $wname $inbox]]]
    [= $mon [?monitor $w]]
    [= $_sp [?receive from=$mon]]
    [= $_ev [?send [child-started name=$name attempt=$attempt] to=$events]]
    [sup--rec-with $rec 'running' $wname $attempt $spawns $mon $w]]]

[?def sup--probe-terminal scope=private impure [returns element] ($rec::map)
  [?let [= $mon $rec/mon]
    [?select
      [case [from $mon $e] [got [term $e]]]
      [case [timeout 0] [none]]]]]

# cancel + bounded wait; emits child-exited/child-abandoned; returns final state string
[?def sup--stop-wait scope=private impure [returns string] ($sleepch $rec::map $events)
  [?let [= $_c [?cancel worker=$rec/w]]
    [= $tries [+ 1 [/ $rec/shutdown-ms 20]]]
    [sup--stop-wait-poll $sleepch $rec $events $tries]]]

[?def sup--stop-wait-poll scope=private impure [returns string] ($sleepch $rec::map $events $tries::int)
  [?let [= $p [sup--probe-terminal $rec]]
    [?match $p
      [case [got]
        [?let [= $_cl [?close $rec/mon]]
          [= $_ev [?send [child-exited name=$rec/name reason=:cancelled] to=$events]]
          'stopped']]
      [else
        [?if [< $tries 1]
          [then [?let [= $_ev [?send [child-abandoned name=$rec/name] to=$events]]
            [= $_cl [?close $rec/mon]]
            'abandoned']]
          [else [?let [= $_zz [?receive from=$sleepch max=1 deadline=20]]
            [= $t2 [- $tries 1]]
            [sup--stop-wait-poll $sleepch $rec $events $t2]]]]]]]]

# bounded-stop every RUNNING child named in $names, honoring $order (a name sequence)
[?def sup--stop-many scope=private impure [returns any] ($st::map $names $order)
  [?let [= $_cp [?check-cancel]]
  [?if [$empty $order]
    [then $st/children]
    [else
      [?let [= $n [$first $order]]
        [= $rest [$tail $order]]
        [= $kids $st/children]
        [= $children2 [?for [in $c $kids]
          [yield [?if [and [= $c/name $n] [and [= $c/state 'running'] [sup--member $names $n]]]
            [then [?let [= $fs [sup--stop-wait $st/sleepch $c $st/events]]
              [sup--rec-state $c $fs]]]
            [else $c]]]]]
        [= $st2 [sup--st-set $st $children2 $st/pends $st/decisions $st/gave-up]]
        [sup--stop-many $st2 $names $rest]]]]]]

# ── the loop ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

[?def sup--loop scope=private impure [returns element] ($st::map)
  [?let [= $msg [?receive from=$st/isub]]
    [?if [sup--is-err $msg]
      [then [?let [= $st2 [sup--stop-all $st]] [stopped]]]
      [else [sup--dispatch $st $msg]]]]]

[?def sup--dispatch scope=private impure [returns element] ($st::map $msg)
  [?let [= $_cp [?check-cancel]]
  [?match $msg
    [case [tick]
      [?let [= $st2 [sup--on-tick $st $msg]]
        [= $st3 [sup--publish-st $st2]]
        [sup--loop-or-die $st3]]]
    [else
      [?let [= $head [$first $msg]]
        [?match $head
          [case [sup-note]
            [?let [= $st2 [sup--on-note $st $msg]]
              [= $st3 [sup--publish-st $st2]]
              [sup--loop-or-die $st3]]]
          [case [sup-op] [sup--on-op $st $msg]]
          [else [sup--loop $st]]]]]]]]

[?def sup--publish-st scope=private impure [returns map] ($st::map)
  [?let [= $_cp [?check-cancel]]
    [= $_ [sup--publish $st/statusch $st/children $st/decisions]]
    $st]]

[?def sup--loop-or-die scope=private impure [returns element] ($st::map)
  [?let [= $_cp [?check-cancel]]
  [?if $st/gave-up
    [then [err code=cx-err:CXER5094 message='E_SUP_RESTART_INTENSITY: restart intensity exceeded — supervisor gave up']]
    [else [sup--loop $st]]]]]

# ── notes ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

[?def sup--on-note scope=private impure [returns map] ($st::map $msg)
  [?let [= $note [$first $msg]]
    [= $name [$concat "" $note@name]]
    [= $wname [$concat "" $note@wname]]
    [= $kids $st/children]
    [= $hits [?for [in $c $kids]
        [where [and [= $c/name $name] [and [= $c/wname $wname] [= $c/state 'running']]]]
        [yield $c]]]
    [?if [< [$count $hits] 1]
      [then $st]
      [else
        [?let [= $cur [$first $hits]]
          [= $outcome $note@outcome]
          [= $panicked [= $outcome :panicked]]
          [= $errs [?for [in $e $msg] [where [sup--is-err $e]] [yield $e]]]
          [; #951 — BOTH :panicked producers pair the note with its [err],
             yet under full-parallel load one note in ~3,200 arrived with an
             EMPTY error filter, and building err-code= from [$first ()] hit
             the engine's (correct) empty-attribute refusal — which crashed
             the WHOLE supervisor loop over one malformed note. Per the #908
             reasoning: never default to "" (that asserts no-cause) — but a
             supervisor dying of a cosmetic attribute refusal is worse than
             an explicit marker. 'cause-unreported' states exactly what is
             known: the child panicked and its cause did not arrive. ]
          [= $ecode [?if $panicked
              [then [?if [< [$count $errs] 1]
                [then 'cause-unreported']
                [else [?let [= $e1 [$first $errs]] [$concat "" $e1@code]]]]]
              [else ""]]]
          [= $ev [?if $panicked
              [then [child-exited name=$name reason=:panicked err-code=$ecode]]
              [else [child-exited name=$name reason=:done]]]]
          [= $_ev [?send $ev to=$st/events]]
          [= $_cl [?close $cur/mon]]
          [= $restart $cur/restart]
          [= $should [?if [= $restart :permanent] [then true]
              [else [?if [= $restart :transient] [then $panicked] [else false]]]]]
          [?if $should
            [then
              [?let [= $children1 [?for [in $c $kids]
                  [yield [?if [= $c/name $name] [then [sup--rec-state $c 'stopped']] [else $c]]]]]
                [= $stx [sup--st-set $st $children1 $st/pends $st/decisions false]]
                [sup--decide $stx $cur]]]
            [else
              [?let [= $children2 [?for [in $c $kids]
                  [yield [?if [= $c/name $name] [then [sup--rec-state $c 'stopped']] [else $c]]]]]
                [sup--st-set $st $children2 $st/pends $st/decisions false]]]]]]]]]

# ── the policy decision ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────

[?def sup--decide scope=private impure [returns map] ($st::map $cur::map)
  [?if [> [+ $st/decisions 1] $st/max-restarts]
    [then [sup--give-up $st]]
    [else
      [?let
        [= $wdur [$time:duration-ms $st/window-ms]]
        [= $wt [$sched:after $wdur $st/inbox]]
        [= $wpend {'kind': 'window' 'timer': [$concat "" $wt@name] 'names': () 'trigger': "" 'attempt': 0 'delay-ms': 0}]
        [= $attempt [+ $cur/attempt 1]]
        [= $delay-ms [sup--backoff-ms $st $attempt]]
        # the affected set, in start order
        [= $kids0 $st/children]
        [= $affected [?if [= $st/strategy :one-for-one]
            [then [$fp:pure $cur/name]]
            [else [?if [= $st/strategy :one-for-all]
              [then [?for [in $c $kids0] [yield $c/name]]]
              [else [sup--tail-names $kids0 $cur/name]]]]]]
        # cancel the other affected running children, reverse start order (never countable)
        [= $others [?for [in $n $affected] [where [not [= $n $cur/name]]] [yield $n]]]
        [= $order [sup--reverse $others]]
        [= $st1 [sup--st-set $st $st/children $st/pends [+ $st/decisions 1] false]]
        [= $children2 [sup--stop-many $st1 $others $order]]
        # the restart set: affected minus :temporary members (marked restarting)
        [= $children3 [?for [in $c $children2]
            [yield [?if [and [sup--member $affected $c/name] [not [= $c/restart :temporary]]]
              [then [sup--rec-state $c 'restarting']]
              [else $c]]]]]
        [= $rnames [?for [in $c $children3] [where [= $c/state 'restarting']] [yield $c/name]]]
        [= $pend0 {'kind': 'restart' 'names': $rnames 'trigger': [$concat "" $cur/name] 'attempt': $attempt 'delay-ms': $delay-ms}]
        [= $st2 [sup--st-set $st1 $children3 $st1/pends $st1/decisions false]]
        [?if [< $delay-ms 1]
          [then [?let [= $stR [sup--do-restart $st2 $pend0]]
            [= $pends2 [sup--append $stR/pends [$fp:pure $wpend]]]
            [sup--st-set $stR $stR/children $pends2 $stR/decisions false]]]
          [else
            [?let [= $ddur [$time:duration-ms $delay-ms]]
              [= $rt [$sched:after $ddur $st/inbox]]
              [= $pend {'kind': 'restart' 'timer': [$concat "" $rt@name] 'names': $rnames
                        'trigger': [$concat "" $cur/name] 'attempt': $attempt 'delay-ms': $delay-ms}]
              [= $pends2 [sup--append $st2/pends ($pend, $wpend)]]
              [sup--st-set $st2 $st2/children $pends2 $st2/decisions false]]]]]]]]

[?def sup--backoff-ms scope=private pure [returns int] ($st::map $attempt::int)
  [?if [= $st/backoff :none]
    [then 0]
    [else [?let [= $p [sup--pow2 [- $attempt 1]]]
      [= $raw [* $st/base-ms $p]]
      [?if [> $raw $st/cap-ms] [then $st/cap-ms] [else $raw]]]]]]

# names of $trigger and every later-started child (start order)
[?def sup--tail-names scope=private pure [returns any] ($children $trigger::string)
  [?if [$empty $children]
    [then ()]
    [else
      [?let [= $h [$first $children]]
        [?if [= $h/name $trigger]
          [then [?for [in $c $children] [yield $c/name]]]
          [else [?let [= $t [$tail $children]] [sup--tail-names $t $trigger]]]]]]]]

[?def sup--give-up scope=private impure [returns map] ($st::map)
  [?let [= $kids $st/children]
    [= $running [?for [in $c $kids] [where [= $c/state 'running']] [yield $c/name]]]
    [= $order [sup--reverse $running]]
    [= $children2 [sup--stop-many $st $running $order]]
    [= $_ev [?send [gave-up restarts=$st/decisions window-ms=$st/window-ms] to=$st/events]]
    [sup--st-set $st $children2 $st/pends $st/decisions true]]]

# ── ticks ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

[?def sup--on-tick scope=private impure [returns map] ($st::map $tick)
  [?let [= $_cp [?check-cancel]]
    [= $tname [$concat "" $tick@timer]]
    [= $allp $st/pends]
    [= $hits [?for [in $p $allp] [where [= [?else $p/timer ""] $tname]] [yield $p]]]
    [?if [< [$count $hits] 1]
      [then $st]
      [else
        [?let [= $hit [$first $hits]]
          [= $pends2 [?for [in $p $allp] [where [not [= [?else $p/timer ""] $tname]]] [yield $p]]]
          [= $st2 [sup--st-set $st $st/children $pends2 $st/decisions false]]
          [?if [= $hit/kind 'window']
            [then [sup--st-set $st2 $st2/children $st2/pends [- $st2/decisions 1] false]]
            [else [?if [= $hit/kind 'restart']
              [then [sup--do-restart $st2 $hit]]
              [else [?if [= $hit/kind 'health']
                [then [sup--on-health $st2 $hit]]
                [else $st2]]]]]]]]]]]

[?def sup--on-health scope=private pure [returns map] ($st::map $hit::map)
  [?let [= $kids $st/children]
    [= $children2 [?for [in $c $kids]
      [yield [?if [and [= $c/name $hit/name] [and [= $c/wname $hit/wname] [= $c/state 'running']]]
        [then [sup--rec-with $c 'running' $c/wname 0 $c/spawns $c/mon $c/w]]
        [else $c]]]]]
    [sup--st-set $st $children2 $st/pends $st/decisions false]]]

[?def sup--do-restart scope=private impure [returns map] ($st::map $pend::map)
  [?let [= $kk $st/children]
    [= $children2 [?for [in $c $kk]
      [yield [?if [and [= $c/state 'restarting'] [sup--member $pend/names $c/name]]
        [then
          [?let [= $att [?if [= $c/name $pend/trigger] [then $pend/attempt] [else [+ $c/attempt 1]]]]
            [= $_ev [?send [child-restarted name=$c/name attempt=$att delay-ms=$pend/delay-ms] to=$st/events]]
            [= $rec2 [sup--spawn $st/sid $st/inbox $st/events $c $att]]
            $rec2]]
        [else $c]]]]]
    # arm the per-child health (attempt-reset) timers for the respawned members
    [= $hpends [?for [in $c $children2]
        [where [and [= $c/state 'running'] [sup--member $pend/names $c/name]]]
        [yield [sup--arm-health $st $c]]]]
    [= $pends2 [sup--append $st/pends $hpends]]
    [sup--st-set $st $children2 $pends2 $st/decisions false]]]

[?def sup--arm-health scope=private impure [returns map] ($st::map $c::map)
  [?let [= $wdur [$time:duration-ms $st/window-ms]]
    [= $ht [$sched:after $wdur $st/inbox]]
    {'kind': 'health' 'timer': [$concat "" $ht@name] 'name': [$concat "" $c/name]
     'wname': [$concat "" $c/wname] 'names': () 'trigger': "" 'attempt': 0 'delay-ms': 0}]]

# ── ops ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

[?def sup--on-op scope=private impure [returns element] ($st::map $msg)
  [?let [= $op [$first $msg]]
    [= $reply [$first $op/reply/*]]
    [= $kind $op@kind]
    [?if [= $kind :status]
      [then [?let [= $snap [sup--snapshot $st/children $st/decisions]]
        [= $_r [?send $snap to=$reply]]
        [sup--loop $st]]]
      [else [?if [= $kind :stop]
        [then [?let [= $st2 [sup--stop-all $st]]
          [= $_p [sup--publish-st $st2]]
          [= $_r [?send [ok] to=$reply]]
          [stopped]]]
        [else [?if [= $kind :start-child]
          [then [sup--op-start-child $st $op $reply]]
          [else [?if [= $kind :stop-child]
            [then [sup--op-stop-child $st $op $reply]]
            [else [sup--loop $st]]]]]]]]]]]

[?def sup--stop-all scope=private impure [returns map] ($st::map)
  [?let [= $_cp [?check-cancel]]
    [= $kids $st/children]
    [= $running [?for [in $c $kids] [where [= $c/state 'running']] [yield $c/name]]]
    [= $order [sup--reverse $running]]
    [= $children2 [sup--stop-many $st $running $order]]
    [= $children3 [?for [in $c $children2]
        [yield [?if [= $c/state 'restarting'] [then [sup--rec-state $c 'stopped']] [else $c]]]]]
    [sup--st-set $st $children3 $st/pends $st/decisions false]]]

[?def sup--op-start-child scope=private impure [returns element] ($st::map $op $reply)
  [?let [= $sp0 $op/spec/*]
    [= $specs [?for [in $s $sp0] [yield $s]]]
    [= $spec [$first $specs]]
    [= $parsed [sup--parse-child $spec]]
    [?if [sup--is-err $parsed]
      [then [?let [= $_r [?send [sup-reply ok=false code=$parsed@code message=$parsed@message] to=$reply]]
        [sup--loop $st]]]
      [else
        [?let [= $name $parsed/name]
          [= $kids $st/children]
          [= $dups [?for [in $c $kids] [where [= $c/name $name]] [yield $c]]]
          [?if [> [$count $dups] 0]
            [then [?let [= $_r [?send [sup-reply ok=false code='cx-err:CXER5091' message='E_SUP_DUPLICATE_CHILD: a child with this name is already present'] to=$reply]]
              [sup--loop $st]]]
            [else
              [?let [= $rec [sup--spawn $st/sid $st/inbox $st/events $parsed 0]]
                [= $recw [$fp:pure $rec]]
                [= $children2 [sup--append $st/children $recw]]
                [= $st2 [sup--st-set $st $children2 $st/pends $st/decisions false]]
                [= $st3 [sup--publish-st $st2]]
                [= $_r [?send [sup-reply ok=true] to=$reply]]
                [sup--loop $st3]]]]]]]]]

[?def sup--op-stop-child scope=private impure [returns element] ($st::map $op $reply)
  [?let [= $name [$concat "" $op@name]]
    [= $kids $st/children]
    [= $hits [?for [in $c $kids] [where [= $c/name $name]] [yield $c]]]
    [?if [< [$count $hits] 1]
      [then [?let [= $_r [?send [sup-reply ok=true value=false] to=$reply]]
        [sup--loop $st]]]
      [else
        [?let [= $st2 [sup--stop-many $st [$fp:pure $name] [$fp:pure $name]]]
          [= $children2 [?for [in $c $st2] [where [not [= $c/name $name]]] [yield $c]]]
          [= $st3 [sup--st-set $st $children2 $st/pends $st/decisions false]]
          [= $st4 [sup--publish-st $st3]]
          [= $_r [?send [sup-reply ok=true value=true] to=$reply]]
          [sup--loop $st4]]]]]]

# ── validation / parsing ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

[?def sup--parse-child scope=private impure [returns any] ($spec)
  [?let [= $_cp [?check-cancel]]
    [= $ok-el [?match $spec [case [child] true] [else false]]]
    [?if [not $ok-el]
      [then [err code=cx-err:CXER5090 message='E_SUP_ARG_INVALID: a child spec must be a [child …] element']]
      [else
        [?let [= $name [$concat "" [?else $spec@name ""]]]
          [= $restart [?else $spec@restart :permanent]]
          [= $shutdown [?else $spec@shutdown ""]]
          [= $fn0 $spec/fn/*]
          [= $fns [?for [in $f $fn0] [yield $f]]]
          [?if [= $name ""]
            [then [err code=cx-err:CXER5090 message='E_SUP_ARG_INVALID: child spec needs name=']]
            [else [?if [< [$count $fns] 1]
              [then [err code=cx-err:CXER5090 message='E_SUP_ARG_INVALID: child spec needs an [fn CALLABLE] child']]
              [else [?if [not [or [= $restart :permanent] [or [= $restart :transient] [= $restart :temporary]]]]
                [then [err code=cx-err:CXER5090 message='E_SUP_ARG_INVALID: restart= must be :permanent | :transient | :temporary']]
                [else
                  [?let [= $sd-ms [?if [= [$concat "" $shutdown] ""] [then 5000]
                      [else [sup--dur-ms $shutdown]]]]
                    [?if [< $sd-ms 0]
                      [then [err code=cx-err:CXER5090 message='E_SUP_ARG_INVALID: shutdown= must be a non-negative duration']]
                      [else {'name': $name 'fn': [$first $fns] 'restart': $restart 'shutdown-ms': $sd-ms
                             'wname': "" 'attempt': 0 'spawns': 0 'state': 'new' 'mon': [none] 'w': [none]}]]]]]]]]]]]]]]

[?def sup--parse-policy scope=private impure [returns any] ($policy)
  [?let [= $_cp [?check-cancel]]
    [= $ok-el [?match $policy [case [policy] true] [else false]]]
    [?if [not $ok-el]
      [then [err code=cx-err:CXER5090 message='E_SUP_ARG_INVALID: policy must be a [policy …] element']]
      [else
        [?let [= $strategy [?else $policy@strategy :one-for-one]]
          [= $max [?else $policy@max-restarts 3]]
          [= $window [?else $policy@window ""]]
          [= $backoff [?else $policy@backoff :none]]
          [= $base [?else $policy@base ""]]
          [= $cap [?else $policy@cap ""]]
          [?if [not [or [= $strategy :one-for-one] [or [= $strategy :one-for-all] [= $strategy :rest-for-one]]]]
            [then [err code=cx-err:CXER5090 message='E_SUP_ARG_INVALID: strategy= must be :one-for-one | :one-for-all | :rest-for-one']]
            [else [?if [< $max 1]
              [then [err code=cx-err:CXER5090 message='E_SUP_ARG_INVALID: max-restarts= must be >= 1']]
              [else [?if [not [or [= $backoff :exp] [= $backoff :none]]]
                [then [err code=cx-err:CXER5090 message='E_SUP_ARG_INVALID: backoff= must be :exp | :none']]
                [else
                  [?let [= $window-ms [?if [= [$concat "" $window] ""] [then 5000] [else [sup--dur-ms $window]]]]
                    [= $base-ms [?if [= [$concat "" $base] ""] [then 100] [else [sup--dur-ms $base]]]]
                    [= $cap-ms [?if [= [$concat "" $cap] ""] [then 10000] [else [sup--dur-ms $cap]]]]
                    [?if [< $window-ms 1]
                      [then [err code=cx-err:CXER5090 message='E_SUP_ARG_INVALID: window= must be a positive duration']]
                      [else [?if [or [< $base-ms 1] [< $cap-ms 1]]
                        [then [err code=cx-err:CXER5090 message='E_SUP_ARG_INVALID: base=/cap= must be positive durations']]
                        [else {'strategy': $strategy 'max-restarts': $max 'window-ms': $window-ms
                               'backoff': $backoff 'base-ms': $base-ms 'cap-ms': $cap-ms}]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]]

# ── alive-check + op round-trip ─────────────────────────────────────────────

[?def sup--alive scope=private impure [returns bool] ($sup)
  [?let [= $wn [$concat "" $sup@worker]]
    [= $wh [?fallback [?worker-handle name=$wn] [recover-with [none]]]]
    [?if [sup--is-err $wh]
      [then false]
      [else
        [?match $wh
          [case [none] false]
          [else
            [?let [= $mon [?monitor $wh]]
              [= $_sp [?receive from=$mon]]
              [= $probe [?select [case [from $mon $e] [got]] [case [timeout 0] [alive]]]]
              [= $_cl [?close $mon]]
              [?match $probe [case [alive] true] [else false]]]]]]]]]

[?def sup--call scope=private impure [returns element] ($sup $kind $name::string $payload $tries::int)
  [?let [= $reply-name [sup--alloc]]
    [= $rch [?channel name=[$concat "cxsup-reply-" $reply-name] buffer=1]]
    [= $op [sup-op kind=$kind name=$name [reply $rch] [spec $payload]]]
    [= $inbox [$first $sup/ctrl/*]]
    [= $opw [$fp:pure $op]]
    [= $_s [?send $opw to=$inbox]]
    [sup--call-wait $sup $rch $tries]]]

[?def sup--call-wait scope=private impure [returns element] ($sup $rch $tries::int)
  [?let [= $batch [?receive from=$rch max=1 deadline=200]]
    [?if [> [$count $batch] 0]
      [then [$first $batch]]
      [else
        [?let [= $alive [sup--alive $sup]]
          [?if [not $alive]
            [then [err code=cx-err:CXER5093 message='E_SUP_CLOSED: the supervisor is stopped']]
            [else [?if [< $tries 1]
              [then [err code=cx-err:CXER5093 message='E_SUP_CLOSED: no reply from the supervision loop']]
              [else [?let [= $t2 [- $tries 1]] [sup--call-wait $sup $rch $t2]]]]]]]]]]]

# ── public surface ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

[?def start scope=public impure [returns element] ($policy $children)
  [?let [= $pol [sup--parse-policy $policy]]
    [= $parsed [?for [in $c $children] [yield [sup--parse-child $c]]]]
    [= $bad [?for [in $p $parsed] [where [sup--is-err $p]] [yield $p]]]
    [?if [sup--is-err $pol]
      [then $pol]
      [else [?if [> [$count $bad] 0]
      [then [$first $bad]]
      [else
        [?let [= $names [?for [in $p $parsed] [yield $p/name]]]
          [= $dups [?for [in $a $names]
              [where [> [$count [?for [in $b $names] [where [= $a $b]] [yield $b]]] 1]]
              [yield $a]]]
          [?if [> [$count $dups] 0]
            [then [err code=cx-err:CXER5091 message='E_SUP_DUPLICATE_CHILD: child names must be unique per supervisor']]
            [else
             # COMPOSITION GATE (RULED: SPF-1(b), issue #895). Everything above
             # is argument validation — pure, and profile-independent: a
             # malformed policy or child spec is a caller bug in every build,
             # so CXER5090/CXER5091 stay its answer everywhere. Composition
             # starts HERE, where the identity, the four channels and the loop
             # worker are minted, and here a missing substrate is the truthful
             # complaint. supervise cannot honour its own contract without
             # sched — backoff delays, the intensity window and per-child
             # attempt-reset are all sched posts — so a no-sched build refuses
             # at composition rather than yielding a supervisor that silently
             # never backs off, never expires its window and never resets
             # attempts.
             [?if [not [sup--has-sched]]
              [then [err code=cx-err:CXER5095 message='E_SUP_NO_SCHED: the local-effect pack `sched` is absent from this build; cx-stdlib/supervise needs it for backoff delays, the intensity window and per-child attempt-reset']]
              [else
              [?let [= $sid [sup--alloc]]
                [= $inbox [?channel name=[$concat "cxsup-" $sid "-inbox"] sharing=independent retention=window keep=1024]]
                [= $events [?channel name=[$concat "cxsup-" $sid "-events"] sharing=independent retention=window keep=256]]
                [= $statusch [?channel name=[$concat "cxsup-" $sid "-status"] sharing=independent retention=window keep=1]]
                [= $sleepch [?channel name=[$concat "cxsup-" $sid "-sleep"] buffer=1]]
                [= $isub [?subscribe from=$inbox]]
                [= $started [?for [in $r $parsed] [yield [sup--spawn $sid $inbox $events $r 0]]]]
                [= $st {'sid': $sid 'inbox': $inbox 'isub': $isub 'events': $events 'statusch': $statusch
                        'sleepch': $sleepch 'strategy': $pol/strategy 'max-restarts': $pol/max-restarts
                        'window-ms': $pol/window-ms 'backoff': $pol/backoff 'base-ms': $pol/base-ms 'cap-ms': $pol/cap-ms
                        'children': $started 'pends': () 'decisions': 0 'gave-up': false}]
                [= $_p [sup--publish-st $st]]
                [= $lname [$concat "cxsup-" $sid "-loop"]]
                [= $w [?worker name=$lname [sup--loop $st]]]
                [= $nkids [$count $started]]
                [supervisor sup=$sid worker=$lname state="running" strategy=$pol/strategy
                  children=$nkids on-close="supervise/stop"
                  __cx_close_id__=$isub@__cx_close_id__
                  [ctrl $inbox] [events-ch $events] [status-ch $statusch]]]]]]]]]]]]]]

[?def stop scope=public impure [returns null] ($sup)
  [?let [= $alive [sup--alive $sup]]
    [?if [not $alive]
      [then null]
      [else
        [?let [= $r [?fallback [sup--call $sup :stop "" "" 100]
            [recover-with [none]]]]
          null]]]]]

[?def start-child scope=public impure [returns element] ($sup $child)
  [?let [= $_cp [?check-cancel]]
    [= $alive [sup--alive $sup]]
    [?if [not $alive]
      [then [err code=cx-err:CXER5093 message='E_SUP_CLOSED: start-child on a stopped supervisor']]
      [else
        [?let [= $r [sup--call $sup :start-child "" $child 100]]
          [?if [sup--is-err $r]
            [then $r]
            [else [?if $r@ok
              [then [ok]]
              [else [err code=$r@code message=$r@message]]]]]]]]]]

[?def stop-child scope=public impure [returns bool] ($sup $name::string)
  [?let [= $_cp [?check-cancel]]
    [= $alive [sup--alive $sup]]
    [?if [not $alive]
      [then [err code=cx-err:CXER5093 message='E_SUP_CLOSED: stop-child on a stopped supervisor']]
      [else
        [?let [= $r [sup--call $sup :stop-child $name "" 100]]
          [?if [sup--is-err $r]
            [then $r]
            [else $r@value]]]]]]]

[?def status scope=public impure [returns element] ($sup)
  [?let [= $alive [sup--alive $sup]]
    [?if [not $alive]
      [then [?let [= $statusch [$first $sup/status-ch/*]]
        [sup--read-cell $statusch]]]
      [else
        [?let [= $r [?fallback [sup--call $sup :status "" "" 100]
            [recover-with [none]]]]
          [?match $r
            [case [supervisor-status] $r]
            [else [?let [= $statusch [$first $sup/status-ch/*]]
              [sup--read-cell $statusch]]]]]]]]]

[?def events scope=public impure [returns element] ($sup)
  [?let [= $alive [sup--alive $sup]]
    [?if [not $alive]
      [then [err code=cx-err:CXER5093 message='E_SUP_CLOSED: events on a stopped supervisor']]
      [else
        [?let [= $evch [$first $sup/events-ch/*]]
          [= $try [?subscribe from=$evch from-pos=0]]
          [?if [sup--is-err $try]
            [then [?subscribe from=$evch from-pos=$try@floor]]
            [else $try]]]]]]]


[; co-located docs. ]
[module-doc name=supervise
  [scope """Restart policies over monitored workers: run a set of named children (each an arity-0 callable spawned as a worker) under a declared policy — strategy (:one-for-one, :one-for-all, :rest-for-one), restart intensity (max-restarts within a window), and per-child exponential backoff — restarting them when they die according to each child's restart type (:permanent, :transient, :temporary). Provides start, stop, dynamic start-child/stop-child, status snapshots, and an observable event stream of the supervisor's own acts. The supervision loop runs in an ordinary worker, so supervisors nest by composition: a give-up terminates the loop with CXER5094 and a parent supervisor monitoring it escalates by policy. Composes workers, monitors, fan-out channels, and sched timers; adds no new concurrency primitive and no capability."""]]
[fn-doc name=start scope=public purity=impure
  [sig """-> element"""]
  [summary """Validate a policy and child specs, spawn the children and the supervision loop, and return the closeable [supervisor] handle."""]
  [example [code """[?lib 'cx-stdlib/supervise' :as sup]
[?let [= $c [?channel name="doc-sup-start" buffer=1]]
[= $s [$sup:start [policy strategy=:one-for-one max-restarts=3]
        ([child name="a" [fn [?fn () [?receive from=$c]]]])]]
[= $ev [$sup:events $s]]
[= $e [?receive from=$ev max=1 deadline=5000]]
[= $_ [$sup:stop $s]]
$e]"""] [expect """([child-started name=a attempt=0])"""]]
]
[fn-doc name=stop scope=public purity=impure
  [sig """-> null"""]
  [summary """Gracefully stop the supervisor: cancel children in reverse start order, each bounded by its shutdown, then stop the loop; idempotent."""]
  [example [code """[?lib 'cx-stdlib/supervise' :as sup]
[?let [= $c [?channel name="doc-sup-stop" buffer=1]]
[= $s [$sup:start [policy strategy=:one-for-one max-restarts=3]
        ([child name="a" [fn [?fn () [?receive from=$c]]]])]]
[= $r1 [$sup:stop $s]]
[= $r2 [$sup:stop $s]]
($r1, $r2)]"""] [expect """(null, null)"""]]
]
[fn-doc name=start-child scope=public purity=impure
  [sig """-> element"""]
  [summary """Add and start a child under the running policy; it joins at the end of start order. Duplicate names refuse CXER5091."""]
  [example [code """[?lib 'cx-stdlib/supervise' :as sup]
[?let [= $c [?channel name="doc-sup-sc" buffer=1]]
[= $c2 [?channel name="doc-sup-sc2" buffer=1]]
[= $s [$sup:start [policy strategy=:one-for-one max-restarts=3]
        ([child name="a" [fn [?fn () [?receive from=$c]]]])]]
[= $kid [child name="b" [fn [?fn () [?receive from=$c2]]]]]
[= $r [$sup:start-child $s $kid]]
[= $st [$sup:status $s]]
[= $rows [$first $st/*]]
[= $_ [$sup:stop $s]]
($r, [$count $rows])]"""] [expect """([ok], 2)"""]]
]
[fn-doc name=stop-child scope=public purity=impure
  [sig """-> bool"""]
  [summary """Cancel (bounded by its shutdown) and REMOVE a child by name — true if it was present, false if unknown (a value; idempotent removal is normal)."""]
  [example [code """[?lib 'cx-stdlib/supervise' :as sup]
[?let [= $c [?channel name="doc-sup-rc" buffer=1]]
[= $s [$sup:start [policy strategy=:one-for-one max-restarts=3]
        ([child name="a" [fn [?fn () [?receive from=$c]]]])]]
[= $r1 [$sup:stop-child $s "a"]]
[= $r2 [$sup:stop-child $s "a"]]
[= $_ [$sup:stop $s]]
($r1, $r2)]"""] [expect """(true, false)"""]]
]
[fn-doc name=status scope=public purity=impure
  [sig """-> element"""]
  [summary """Read a [supervisor-status] snapshot — restarts-in-window plus each child's name, state (running|restarting|abandoned|stopped), and attempt count; stays readable after stop."""]
  [example [code """[?lib 'cx-stdlib/supervise' :as sup]
[?let [= $c [?channel name="doc-sup-st" buffer=1]]
[= $s [$sup:start [policy strategy=:one-for-one max-restarts=3]
        ([child name="a" [fn [?fn () [?receive from=$c]]]])]]
[= $st [$sup:status $s]]
[= $_ [$sup:stop $s]]
$st]"""] [expect """[supervisor-status restarts-in-window=0 ([child name=a state=running attempts=0])]"""]]
]
[fn-doc name=events scope=public purity=impure
  [sig """-> element"""]
  [summary """Subscribe to the supervisor's own acts — child-started/child-exited/child-restarted/child-abandoned/gave-up — as a standard fan-out subscription replayed from the retained floor."""]
  [example [code """[?lib 'cx-stdlib/supervise' :as sup]
[?let [= $c [?channel name="doc-sup-ev" buffer=4]]
[= $s [$sup:start [policy strategy=:one-for-one max-restarts=3]
        ([child name="a" [fn [?fn () [?receive from=$c]]]])]]
[= $ev [$sup:events $s]]
[= $e0 [?receive from=$ev max=1 deadline=5000]]
[= $_k [?send [go] to=$c]]
[= $e1 [?receive from=$ev max=1 deadline=5000]]
[= $_ [$sup:stop $s]]
($e0, $e1)]"""] [expect """(([child-started name=a attempt=0]), ([child-exited name=a reason=:done]))"""]]
]
